ven  reach the end of the game the first time  you play if you play on medium  difficulty you see lightning returns  likes to waste your time and it does so  and how it handles exploration as you  complete certain side quests others may  open up but you may not know where and  when they do so the game invites you to  return to regions again and again  seeking out new activities and chasing  MacGuffins only to punish you with time  loss if there's nothing to be found  should the world end before you complete  your main quests you have to start over  but you do keep all of your equipment  and enhancements new game+ style  lightning returns also wastes your time  by forcing you to lose an in-game hour  whenever you escape from battle you  might be well equipped for the creatures  in the vicinity only to discover that  you're not powerful enough for the boss  that concludes your quest and be forced  to escape the combat system encourages  you to experiment but the time limit  punishes you for it you want to be saved  time you met you later  the combat does have its bright spots  however at the heart of battle are  combat templates called schemata  schemata in turn are attached to the  outfits lightening wears  she can wear up to three at any time and  switch between them at will during  battle not only the various outfits have  their own attributes but so do the  weapons attacks and accessories you can  equip to them there are countless ways  to fine tune your schemata and playing  around with the possibilities as  lightning returns most interesting and  most enjoyable element lightning  skitters across the battlefield as you  unleash various attacks each attack  costs a certain number of active Time  battle points and the ATB meter  replenishes more slowly than you use it  up as a result you must switch between  schemata frequently as well as block  effectively to stagger enemies and avoid  damage sadly that blocking mechanic is a  big problem to avoid the most damage 